  "rationale": "After the canonical “Once upon a time,” opening, the target is a person name, but the model still assigns the largest probability to <END>. The gradient already raises Ben's comma-conditioned weight, yet the broad punctuation-conditioned <END> rule remains dominant. Add moderate, equal mass for every available proper-name candidate only after this recognizable opening, rather than globally weakening <END> after punctuation, where it may be appropriate after terminal punctuation. This proposes a class-level continuation and does not treat Ben as uniquely determined. A continuation other than a name after this opener remains possible, and the limited vocabulary and single observation do not establish that every such context must introduce a person."
